  "solution": [
    "Because the tracks are parallel, angle \\(BEF\\) (48°) and angle \\(CFE\\) are alternate interior angles, so angle \\(CFE = 48^{\\circ}\\).",
    "Angle \\(DFE\\) forms a straight line with angle \\(CFE\\), so \\(x = 180 - 48 = 132\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "P=figure['points']\nd=lambda a,b: sqrt((P[a][0]-P[b][0])**2+(P[a][1]-P[b][1])**2)\nang=lambda a,v,b: N(acos(((P[a][0]-P[v][0])*(P[b][0]-P[v][0])+(P[a][1]-P[v][1])*(P[b][1]-P[v][1]))/(d(a,v)*d(b,v)))*180/pi)\nassert P['A'][1]==P['B'][1] and P['C'][1]==P['D'][1]\nassert abs(ang('B','E','F')-48)<0.1\nans=180-48\nassert abs(ang('D','F','E')-ans)<0.1\nassert Rational(spr_answers[0])==ans==132\n",
